     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Artemis I Launch</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
   <dc:rights>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">(NASA/Joel Kowsky)&#xA;&#xA;For copyright and restrictions refer to -Â http://www.nasa.gov/multimedia/guidelines/index.html</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:rights>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">NASAâ€™s Space Launch System rocket carrying the Orion spacecraft launches on the Artemis I flight test, Wednesday, Nov. 16, 2022, from Launch Complex 39B at NASAâ€™s Kennedy Space Center in Florida. NASAâ€™s Artemis I mission is the first integrated flight test of the agencyâ€™s deep space exploration systems: the Orion spacecraft, Space Launch System (SLS) rocket, and ground systems. SLS and Orion launched at 1:47 a.m. EST, from Launch Pad 39B at the Kennedy Space Center. Photo Credit: (NASA/Joel Kowsky)</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:subject>
    <rdf:Bag>
     <rdf:li>Artemis</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>Artemis I</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>Artemis I Launch</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>Cape Canaveral</rdf:li>
